      </div>
      <p class="teacher-hero-note">{{LESSONS}} lessons · {{PREREQS}} prerequisite tasks · Worked teaching notes</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="teacher-model" aria-labelledby="teacherModelTitle">
      <figcaption><span class="teacher-model-kicker">A model worth talking about</span><strong id="teacherModelTitle">Same relationship. New scale.</strong></figcaption>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 380 202" role="img" aria-label="A ratio of two teal squares to three outlined squares scales by two to four teal squares and six outlined squares.">
        <g fill="#075e60"><rect x="26" y="26" width="30" height="30" rx="5"/><rect x="64" y="26" width="30" height="30" rx="5"/></g>
        <g fill="#fff" stroke="#152c40" stroke-width="2"><rect x="26" y="72" width="30" height="30" rx="5"/><rect x="64" y="72" width="30" height="30" rx="5"/><rect x="102" y="72" width="30" height="30" rx="5"/></g>
        <path d="M158 64H206m-7-7 7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="#152c40" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="181" y="43" text-anchor="middle" fill="#152c40" font-size="17" font-weight="700">× 2</text>
        <g fill="#075e60"><rect x="226" y="26" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="257" y="26" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="288" y="26" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="319" y="26" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/></g>
        <g fill="#fff" stroke="#152c40" stroke-width="2"><rect x="226" y="66" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="257" y="66" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="288" y="66" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="226" y="97" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="257" y="97" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/><rect x="288" y="97" width="25" height="25" rx="4"/></g>
        <text x="79" y="155" text-anchor="middle" fill="#152c40" font-size="22" font-weight="700">2 : 3</text><text x="282" y="155" text-anchor="middle" fill="#152c40" font-size="22" font-weight="700">4 : 6</text>
        <text x="190" y="188" text-anchor="middle" fill="#405568" font-size="13">Both quantities change by the same factor.</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Ask: <strong>What changes? What stays the same?</strong></p>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap teacher-routine" aria-label="A short teaching routine">
    <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Check &amp; listen</strong>One prompt. Every student explains.</p></div>
    <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Model &amp; connect</strong>Use a representation to test the idea.</p></div>
    <div><span>03</span><p><strong>Practice &amp; revisit</strong>Choose a next step from the evidence.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section protocol-section teacher-only" id="protocolSection">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="card protocol">
      <div class="protocol-head">
        <h2>
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
          A routine for responsive teaching
        </h2>
        <span class="tag">Check → Diagnose → Practice → Revisit</span>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-n">1</div>
          <h3>The Day Before · 1 Minute</h3>
          <p>Open tomorrow's lesson card. Note whether the four prerequisite skills stem from elementary grades (Gr 2–5) or spiral from earlier Grade 6 units. Identify the foundational hurdle before instruction begins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-n">2</div>
          <h3>First 2 Minutes of Class</h3>
          <p>Press <strong>Project</strong> on the lesson card. Display the quick check on your projector or smartboard. Students write answers on individual whiteboards. Use forms A, B, or C across class periods.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-n">3</div>
          <h3>Right After · Decide</h3>
          <p>Open the Answer &amp; Teaching Notes. If the room missed it, run the scripted 4–6 min reteach. If a few students struggle, assign Practice Studio (Foundation / Connect / Extend) or run the Partner Lab.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Listen for the strategy, not just the answer.</strong> Use a quick check as one piece of evidence.
        Ask students to explain or model their thinking before choosing support. Accurate, flexible reasoning matters more than speed.
      </div>

      <!--__ORIGIN__-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

